159
00:21:14,643 --> 00:21:15,664
and we have been brought low.

160
00:21:16,905 --> 00:21:25,773
Not only have we failed to accomplish a single remarkable quality, where we are afflicted by all manner of suffering.

161
00:21:27,235 --> 00:21:29,277
Since that is so, reflect

162
00:21:30,037 --> 00:21:36,701
I will now free myself, however I can, from the mire of these difficult, conflicting thoughts.

163
00:21:37,621 --> 00:21:45,445
And even if, just for a single instant, focus on the Tathagata's body, which is of such great merit and significance.

164
00:21:46,146 --> 00:21:52,809
In doing so, I shall achieve the yogas of calm abiding and insight in their proper way.

165
00:21:53,830 --> 00:21:57,512
And so here, we're taught to reflect upon

166
00:21:59,497 --> 00:22:02,879
the nature of discursive thought.

167
00:22:04,140 --> 00:22:10,764
When we reflect genuinely, honestly upon them, what have they brought us?

168
00:22:10,924 --> 00:22:12,726
What good have they brought us?

169
00:22:14,006 --> 00:22:26,975
If we were to consider ourselves, if we were to consider our mind and the discursive thoughts running therein, let's say we were to give them form, they probably wouldn't fit in this temple, would they?

170
00:22:29,008 --> 00:22:38,770
