And then for the actual practice, one is encouraged to place in front of you, at whatever height and position is comfortable to you, a beautiful and pleasing image of the Tathagata Buddha, the King of the Shakyas.

218
00:30:20,855 --> 00:30:25,258
And this image should be one that has been drawn correctly by a skilled artist.

219
00:30:26,910 --> 00:30:36,636
And, with the power of aspiration, recall the Tathagata's blessings, and by reciting the essence of causation mantra, consecrate the image.

220
00:30:37,116 --> 00:30:42,880
Having done this, place it at whatever distance is right for you to look at.

221
00:30:43,840 --> 00:30:50,644
And this distance should be one that is not too close, nor should it be too far away.

222
00:30:50,664 --> 00:30:55,307
It should be placed at a position that is just right for you.

