When it comes to the image of the Buddha, we generally use a picture of the Bodhgaya image of the Buddha, the Bodhgaya statue.

230
00:31:43,751 --> 00:31:49,776
And so if you look behind me, you'll see a wonderful representation of Buddha Shakyamuni.

231
00:31:49,816 --> 00:31:53,619
So this is based on the Bodhgaya Buddha image.

232
00:31:54,520 --> 00:32:05,186
And so this image is one that is perfect in every way, and if you have a representative of that, that is pleasing to the eye, they should then place it in front of you.

233
00:32:06,287 --> 00:32:15,592
Not too high, because that will force you to look upwards, neither too low, because that would force you to look downwards, but at exactly the right height for you.

