.

286
00:39:19,468 --> 00:39:19,488
.

287
00:39:47,023 --> 00:39:54,471
And so essentially, bringing to mind the Buddha to the best of one's ability.

288
00:39:54,511 --> 00:40:02,500
Now, mention is made here of the major and minor marks of perfection, which are an external display of the inner qualities of omniscience.

289
00:40:03,301 --> 00:40:06,345
Even if you can't bring each and every one of them to mind,

290
00:40:06,885 --> 00:40:14,709
As much as you are able, try to bring those particular qualities to mind and allow them to permeate your being.

291
00:40:15,450 --> 00:40:20,592
And there through, generate an appreciation for the Buddha.

292
00:40:21,193 --> 00:40:23,254
Reflect upon the activities of the Buddha

293
00:40:23,854 --> 00:40:37,824
as we've seen and as we can read in the discourses of the awakened one, how his very kind of sitting down, getting up, moving and so forth, brings inconceivable direct and indirect benefit to sentient beings.

294
00:40:39,065 --> 00:40:45,130
So accordingly, we should reflect then upon these extraordinary activities and the benefit that they bring.

295
00:40:45,670 --> 00:40:58,316
bringing them to mind will infuse the mind with faith and devotion, which will accordingly bring about a kind of natural clarity and pliancy of mind, a wholesomeness, if you will.

296
00:41:17,103 --> 00:41:26,879
So we next move on to the actual focusing of our attention on this image of the Buddha.

297
00:41:27,259 --> 00:41:27,640
We read,

298
00:41:29,525 --> 00:41:48,235
Then, without your attention being too tightly or too loosely focused, but rather in a leisurely manner without losing mindfulness and attentiveness, focus the mind continuously on the appearance of the Tathagata's form.

299
00:41:50,022 --> 00:41:50,042
.

300
00:42:11,178 --> 00:42:17,423
And we read, distance in yourself from any thought other than the object of your focus.

301
00:42:18,124 --> 00:42:21,086
Settle your attention only on the Buddha's form.

302
00:42:21,887 --> 00:42:28,472
And so here, one should acknowledge that there may be other thoughts running through one's being.

303
00:42:29,013 --> 00:42:31,955
However, at this time, one shouldn't pay them any heed.

304
00:42:32,435 --> 00:42:39,281
Rather, one should make a pledge to continually place one's attention on the form of the Buddha.

305
00:42:41,216 --> 00:42:48,540
And by doing so, eventually you will focus single-pointedly or one-pointedly without interruption for as long as you like.

306
00:42:48,620 --> 00:42:51,021
Essentially then, practice progressively

307
00:43:11,807 --> 00:43:20,555
and pass through the nine methods of mental abiding until you achieve the one-pointedness of mind of the desire realm.

308
00:43:20,875 --> 00:43:32,024
And so here, mention is made then of nine methods or nine mental placements that one passes through in pursuit of the single-pointedness of mind of the desire realm.

309
00:43:33,245 --> 00:43:33,265
.

310
00:43:33,305 --> 00:43:33,325
.

311
00:43:33,345 --> 00:43:33,385
.

312
