346
00:47:25,112 --> 00:47:40,001
Now, when placing one's attention on the form of the Buddha, it can be that one is faced with difficulties in sustaining the image upon which we are focusing.

347
00:47:40,441 --> 00:47:40,922
attention.

348
00:47:41,362 --> 00:47:56,119
And so here are some methods that we can utilize to overcome the difficulties or the distractions that we are faced with whilst not leaving the image that we are focused upon single-pointedly.

349
00:47:56,199 --> 00:47:56,519
We read

350
00:47:58,081 --> 00:48:16,335
you can look at and focus upon the body in general, or in order to obtain the noble dharma and pacify dullness, focus primarily on the ushnisha, the crown protrusion on the Buddha's head, the limit of which is impossible to see.

351
00:48:17,035 --> 00:48:24,803
And so here the way of focusing on these particular parts of the body is to kind of zoom in and zoom out.

352
00:48:25,004 --> 00:48:35,515
Zooming in when you need to address a particular distraction and zoom out and perhaps refocusing and then zooming in on a different part of the body when

353
00:48:36,195 --> 00:48:40,537
beset with a different distraction.

354
00:48:41,317 --> 00:48:47,440
So accordingly, then, the first one is given, to look at the crown of the head, at the ushnisha.

355
00:48:48,581 --> 00:48:52,422
Alternately, in order to obtain samadhi and pacify...

356
00:48:52,462 --> 00:48:59,786
So anyway, the first one, where you look to the top of the Buddha's image, is to pacify dullness.

357
00:49:00,846 --> 00:49:17,456
On the other hand, in order to obtain samadhi and pacify agitation, we are then encouraged to concentrate, or rather zoom in, on the enlightened mind's glorious knot, which is between the breasts of the Buddha, at the Buddha's heart center, as you read.

358
00:49:18,737 --> 00:49:44,295
or to accomplish great merit and gain happiness you can concentrate on the appearance of the coil of hair between the Buddha's eyebrows which is as white as snow or conch and curls to the right and in order to make the great melodious sound of the Dharma pervade the whole world and to benefit sentient beings by teaching the Dharma

359
00:49:45,075 --> 00:49:57,538
One should fix your mind or fix your attention on the form of the throat, the source of 60 qualities of melodious speech, the conch of the Dharma with its three lines.

360
00:49:57,558 --> 00:50:04,619
So accordingly, the throat of the Buddha, there are three lines or three creases, if you like.

361
00:50:05,639 --> 00:50:12,941
And accordingly, wherever it is you feel inclined to focus, concentrate your mind there unwaveringly.

362
00:50:14,942 --> 00:50:14,962
.

363
00:50:34,553 --> 00:50:46,919
Now when practicing calm abiding meditation or settling of mind that leads to calm abiding meditation, one will pass through five meditative experiences.

364
00:50:48,559 --> 00:50:54,422
We read, when focusing your mind like this, at the very beginning it is like catching a snake.

365
00:50:55,222 --> 00:51:02,886
The mind is so wild and untamed that the first stage of meditation is called the experience

366
00:51:03,666 --> 00:51:05,747
of movement like a waterfall.

367
00:51:32,105 --> 00:51:41,447
It's important here to reflect on the experience of some when practicing calm abiding meditation.

368
00:51:42,228 --> 00:51:46,188
It can be that we feel that I'm getting worse and worse.

369
00:51:46,929 --> 00:51:48,749
Mind is getting more and more agitated.

370
00:51:49,709 --> 00:51:52,470
There's more and more kind of discursive thought passing through.

371
00:51:53,190 --> 00:51:54,590
But I don't think this is the case.

372
00:51:55,711 --> 00:51:56,791
What usually happens

373
00:51:57,671 --> 00:51:59,212
is we don't really look within.

374
00:51:59,872 --> 00:52:08,417
We're so focused on the objects that are proffered to us through the sense doors, we do not take adequate time to look within.

375
00:52:08,758 --> 00:52:23,366
And when we do, rather than kind of the finding that the mind is as peaceful as we'd like to believe it actually is, when that calmness and clarity comes through taking the time to allow ourselves the opportunity to look within,

376
00:52:24,663 --> 00:52:32,448
what we find is agitation and an incredible amount of thought that's always been there, it's just that we're noticing it for the first time.

377
00:52:43,734 --> 00:52:43,774
.

378
00:52:43,814 --> 00:52:43,874
.

379
00:52:43,914 --> 00:52:43,974
.

380
00:52:44,014 --> 00:52:44,034
.

381
00:53:02,801 --> 00:53:02,961
.

382
00:53:03,021 --> 00:53:03,101
.

383
00:53:03,121 --> 00:53:03,141
.

384
00:53:25,200 --> 00:53:35,805
As we read, at this stage you have the impression that your mind is in constant motion from the sutra requested by Subahu.

385
00:53:37,646 --> 00:53:50,572
This mind is like lightning, wind and clouds, like the waves of a giant ocean, cunning, indulging in everything it desires, moving, straying.

386
00:53:51,613 --> 00:53:52,033
Reflect.

387
00:53:52,813 --> 00:53:53,974
I must certainly tame it.

388
00:53:55,542 --> 00:54:09,819
Accordingly, one should reflect, since all sentient beings have fallen under the sway of this completely distracted mind, I will persevere without giving into laziness, come what may.

389
00:54:11,020 --> 00:54:14,483
For if one perseveres, there is nothing one cannot accomplish.

390
00:54:15,543 --> 00:54:19,826
Accordingly, endeavor to maintain the focus for as long as you can.

391
00:54:20,567 --> 00:54:31,434
And, by persevering in this way, discursive thoughts, which were so apparent and rough, wild and turbulent, will settle down slightly after a while.

392
00:54:33,163 --> 00:54:41,588
But there will still be the busyness of the many different thoughts, a bubbling stream of restless mental activity.

393
00:54:42,408 --> 00:54:53,455
This recognition is the second meditation experience of attainment, and it is likened to a river flowing through a narrow canyon.

394
00:54:55,920 --> 00:54:55,980
.

395
00:54:56,020 --> 00:54:56,040
.

396
00:54:56,080 --> 00:54:56,120
.

397
00:54:56,160 --> 00:54:56,220
.

398
00:54:56,240 --> 00:54:56,260
.

399
00:55:22,829 --> 00:55:37,793
The second example of a river flowing through a narrow canyon is used because although a river running through said canyon is still very turbulent and noisy, it is a little slower than a waterfall.

400
00:55:39,533 --> 00:55:50,816
If you keep persevering and continue the practice, then you will feel that inwardly the mind's thoughts are slowing down and you are able to remain with the object of focus.

401
00:55:51,796 --> 00:55:52,156
However,

402
00:55:53,116 --> 00:56:07,079
If you carefully examine, you will see that you are still involved in a continuous stream of many subtle conceptual thoughts or discursive thoughts.

403
00:56:08,079 --> 00:56:18,842
At this point, you've reached the third experience called the experience of familiarization, and it is likened to a gently flowing stream.

404
00:56:21,008 --> 00:56:21,088
.

405
00:56:21,108 --> 00:56:21,128
.

406
00:56:56,910 --> 00:57:04,900
When you look at a stream from afar, it seems to be still, and you cannot tell that it is moving.

407
00:57:06,121 --> 00:57:10,767
But when you get up close, you'll see that it is moving, alight and rippling.

408
00:57:13,583 --> 00:57:26,117
Accordingly then, from this point on, if you don't stop persevering, but keep on striving, you will have less hardship and suffering than before.

409
00:57:27,218 --> 00:57:29,621
So exert yourself continuously, we are told.

410
00:57:30,802 --> 00:57:37,846
By practicing like this, even the movement of subtle conceptual thoughts will be pacified.

411
00:57:38,647 --> 00:57:43,709
And as long as you have the conditioning for the focus, you will be able to remain as long as you like.

412
00:57:45,250 --> 00:57:49,693
Yet this does not mean that you are completely impervious to circumstances.

413
00:57:50,654 --> 00:58:03,866
And this then is the fourth meditation experience called the experience of stability, which is like an ocean free from waves, since the mind abides and is stable.

414
00:58:05,868 --> 00:58:05,948
.

415
00:58:06,008 --> 00:58:06,068
.

416
00:58:06,088 --> 00:58:06,108
.

417
00:58:06,148 --> 00:58:06,168
.

418
00:58:35,977 --> 00:58:53,121
Having reached this far, then without having to undergo great hardships, the fifth meditation experience, perfection, which is likened to a mountain, will arise as long as you continue to familiarize yourself with the state over time.

419
00:58:54,461 --> 00:58:57,782
And this then is synonymous with effortless engagement.

420
00:58:59,433 --> 00:59:07,675
The mind naturally mixes with whatever you focus on, and without the need for any effort, remains steadily wherever you want it to.

421
00:59:08,776 --> 00:59:13,877
Conceptual or discursive thoughts no longer have the power to shake your mind.

422
00:59:14,157 --> 00:59:20,459
And this is the accomplishment, is what is called the one-pointedness of a mind of the desire realm.

423
00:59:21,560 --> 00:59:21,980
Thank you.

424
00:59:36,724 --> 00:59:44,548
And so when we reflect upon the result, which is the one-pointedness or single-pointedness of a mind of the desire realm.

425
00:59:45,609 --> 00:59:55,474
So this is the result of a way of training in Khayamavadi meditation, which is levied out according to five experiences of meditation.

426
00:59:58,655 --> 01:00:04,961
And so you will recall, I went through earlier the nine mental placements, the result is the same.

427
01:00:05,041 --> 01:00:08,403
So these are just different ways of delineation.

428
01:00:17,068 --> 01:00:17,148
.

429
01:00:17,168 --> 01:00:17,248
.

430
01:00:17,268 --> 01:00:17,328
.

431
01:00:17,368 --> 01:00:17,468
.

432
01:00:17,508 --> 01:00:17,528
.

433
01:00:44,288 --> 01:00:46,809
At this time, various experiences resulting from the mind's abiding will also arise.

434
01:00:47,490 --> 01:00:52,492
When you have become familiar with this state, mind and body are said to become supple.

435
01:01:16,096 --> 01:01:29,144
As body and mind become workable in this way, whatever objects of focus you settle the mind upon, even if you remain for several days, there is no sense at all of either the body or the mind being unable to cope.

436
01:01:30,225 --> 01:01:36,569
The body feels as light as cotton and the mind is pervaded by the bliss of vivid clarity.

437
01:01:37,870 --> 01:01:55,100
this subtleness is rough and heavy at first and has a sense of solidity but with familiarity the heaviness fades and there arises an unwavering some shamatha that is extremely fine and clear like a shadow

438
01:01:56,442 --> 01:02:01,409
a mind of meditative concentration that is in accord with the main part of the practice.

439
01:02:02,410 --> 01:02:09,561
This kind of meditation has the name shamatha, calm abiding, since it is a mind endowed with subtleness.

440
01:02:10,562 --> 01:02:10,582
.

441
01:02:10,642 --> 01:02:10,742
.

442
01:02:10,762 --> 01:02:10,782
.

443
01:02:10,842 --> 01:02:10,922
.

444
01:02:10,942 --> 01:02:10,962
.

445
01:02:39,347 --> 01:02:50,422
this mind also corresponds to the aspect of the first meditative absorptions capable preparatory stage

446
01:02:52,120 --> 01:03:04,812
There is nothing that this kind of meditative concentration is incapable of, be it meditation with a conceptual focus or meditation without concepts, as in the meditations on emptiness and the like.

447
01:03:05,593 --> 01:03:10,257
There are several ways of counting the stages of accomplishing shamatha.

448
01:03:17,262 --> 01:03:20,684
such as the four mental engagements or the six powers.

449
01:03:21,024 --> 01:03:24,086
But essentially, they are all included in the following.

450
01:03:24,947 --> 01:03:34,312
The mind remains totally concentrated with mindfulness and attentiveness for as long as possible on whichever objects you choose to focus.

451
01:03:35,193 --> 01:03:42,117
And as you familiarize yourself with this, the five meditative experiences will arrive.

452
01:03:49,389 --> 01:03:49,449
.

453
01:03:49,469 --> 01:03:49,509
.

454
01:03:49,529 --> 01:03:49,589
.

455
01:03:49,609 --> 01:03:49,629
.

456
01:04:20,942 --> 01:04:37,461
Accordingly, when you have accomplished shamatha, karma-abiding meditation in this way, the strength of the mind's workability, pliancy if you will, gives the body a gleaming complexion and makes it comfortable and strong.

457
01:04:38,662 --> 01:04:40,625
The mind too becomes clear and lucid.

458
01:04:41,325 --> 01:04:43,826
and settles on any object of your choice.

459
01:04:44,626 --> 01:04:48,528
Body and mind are saturated with immeasurable joy and bliss.

460
01:04:48,968 --> 01:04:58,752
The afflictions are reduced and you'll have an experience concordant with the extraordinary joy of inner solitude.

461
01:04:59,633 --> 01:05:13,168
By the strength of the merit of practicing this way, with the focus on the form of the Buddha and through the Buddha's blessing, you'll come to see the Buddha, either in actuality or in dreams, receiving the Dharma and all sorts of excellent qualities will arise.

462
01:05:19,857 --> 01:05:29,540
And so accordingly, focusing on the form of the Buddha and through the Buddha's blessing, you, the meditator, will ultimately come to see the Buddha either in actuality or in dreams.

463
01:05:45,485 --> 01:05:48,366
And thereby, you will receive Dharma teachings and so on.

464
01:05:48,846 --> 01:05:55,628
And all sorts of wondrous, excellent qualities of various sorts will arise within you.

465
01:05:56,428 --> 01:06:02,910
And so accordingly then, I've given you the teaching, a brief teaching on the method of calm abiding.

466
01:06:12,334 --> 01:06:27,629
And so you see, by this, practicing in this way, you'll notice, the text reads, when you have accomplished shamatha in this way, the strength of the mind's workability gives the body a gleaming complexion.

467
01:06:28,090 --> 01:06:29,391
And so you can save on makeup.

468
01:06:40,779 --> 01:06:58,888
If you look around here at the faces of all of our teachers, you can see in the radiance of their faces, the kind of natural radiance in their faces is reflective of the inner qualities of realization and experience.

